# Pre-commit: the two checks a commit can be stopped for, and only those.
#
# This file was a single comment saying the full gates run in CI, which meant
# there was no pre-commit gate at all — and `husky` was not a dependency, so the
# hook was never installed either. A hook that is not installed is worse than no
# hook: `ls .husky` shows a gate, and a reviewer trusts the directory rather than
# the contents.
#
# Deliberately small, and deliberately not `pnpm verify`:
#
#   - `security:secrets` — the working tree only, and it is fast. A commit that
#     adds a credential is the one thing a commit hook is uniquely placed to stop,
#     because it is the last moment before the value is in history, where removing
#     it is a rewrite rather than a delete.
#   - `format:check` on the staged files only. Formatting the whole repository on
#     every commit is slow enough that people reach for `--no-verify`, and a gate
#     that gets bypassed is not a gate.
#
# NOT here, on purpose:
#
#   - the history scan (`pnpm security:secrets:history`). It is proportional to the
#     commit count, which is the wrong cost for an interactive hook. CI runs it.
#   - `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`. They run in CI on every push, and
#     putting them here only buys a slower commit.
#
# To skip once, deliberately: `git commit --no-verify`. If that becomes routine,
# delete this file rather than debugging it.

pnpm security:secrets

staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR)
if [ -n "$staged" ]; then
  # Batched, because the whole list in one argv overflows the Windows command
  # line at around 8k characters. A 200-file commit is an ordinary size, and a
  # hook that cannot run on Windows is a gate that gets --no-verify'd.
  #
  # --ignore-unknown, because an explicit file list bypasses the globs in
  # `format:check`: without it prettier errors on every .sql migration and
  # every extensionless dotfile in the commit, and the gate fails on a tree
  # that is correctly formatted.
  printf '%s\n' "$staged" | xargs -d '\n' -n 40 pnpm exec prettier --check --ignore-unknown || {
    echo ""
    echo "Staged files are not formatted. Run \`pnpm format\` and stage the result."
    exit 1
  }
fi
